# JavaScript Style

- Use named `function` declarations. Do not use anonymous functions or arrow syntax (`=>`).
- Handlers take a `response` argument and return a result.
- Prefer jQuery over vanilla DOM APIs.
- Prefer promises (`.then` / `.catch`) and callbacks. Do not use `async`/`await`.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
$('.nav-link').each(() => { $(this).addClass('active') })
async function load() {
  const data = await fetch(url).then(r => r.json())
}

// ✅ GOOD
$('.nav-link').each(each_navlink)
function each_navlink() {
  $(this).addClass('active')
}

function get_json(url) {
  return fetch(url).then(done).catch(caught(url))
  function done(response) {
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error('HTTP ' + response.status)
    }
    return response.json()
  }
}
```
